  "worked_solution": "We model the growth of the cultivated area using the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}A}{\\text{d}t}=0.08A.\n$$\n\nThe solution to this equation is\n\n$$\nA(t)={A}_{0}\\,{e}^{0.08t},\n$$\n\nwhere ${A}_{0}$ is the initial cultivated area.\n\nLet ${t}_{1}$ be the time when the cultivated area has increased by $40%.$ That is,\n\n$$\nA({t}_{1})=1.4{A}_{0}.\n$$\n\nWe solve the above equation for ${t}_{1},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A({t}_{1}) & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.08\\cdot {t}_{1}} \\\\ 1.4{A}_{0} & ={A}_{0}{e}^{0.08{t}_{1}} \\\\ 1.4 & ={e}^{0.08{t}_{1}} \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1.4) & =\\operatorname{ln}\u2061({e}^{0.08{t}_{1}}) \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1.4) & =0.08{t}_{1} \\\\ {t}_{1} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}\u2061(1.4)}{0.08} \\\\ {t}_{1} & \u22484.205\\,9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRounding to the nearest decimal place, we conclude that it takes $4.2$ years for the cultivated area to increase by $40%.$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
